WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.200
Hello.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.420
Right now we’re at…

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.120
Suvarnabhumi Airport.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.000
We’re heading to Hong Kong.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.780
It’s our first fan meeting in Hong Kong.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.140
How are you feeling, Bonnie?

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.600
I feel so, so happy.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.980
Super happy. I want to go to Disneyland.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.820
Whoa, she wants to go to Disneyland, everyone.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:33.980
Yes, everyone.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.440
Sorry, internet people. It’s me who wasn’t free.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.640
No, it’s because we had to take an early flight.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.140
Everyone, please don’t gang up and stomp on me.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.440
Nah, everyone is cheering for you.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.500
Last night I was filming at Khao Yai. 
I finished around midnight.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:50.480
Oh?

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.980
Didn’t get home until after 3 a.m.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.440
And I had to wash my hair.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.560
So? Were you sad?

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.860
Sad. I cried.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.400
When I was washing my hair, 
while taking out the pins,

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.260
I kept pulling out pins and 
tearing up at the same time.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.860
So, you cried.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.560
It’s because I was sleepy.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.180
But once we get to Hong Kong, we’ll be energized.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:09.960
Mhm.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:10.700
We’ll go to a temple.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:11.880
Yes.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.220
To boost our energy first.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.400
Yes, that’s right.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.260
Okay, we’ll go to Che Kung Temple to recharge.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.800
And the next day we’ll be ready to meet the fans.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.440
I might still be half-asleep 
because I only slept two hours.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.120
Yes, but tomorrow when we see you all, 
we’ll give you everything we’ve got.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.200
See you in Hong Kong.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.640
Bye-bye.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.940
See you in Hong Kong!

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.100
Right now we’re still in Thailand, everyone.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:40.620
(No!)

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.220
The sign says “Cashier.”

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.080
We’ve been flying forever…

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.800
Now we’re at Che Kung Temple.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.820
Yes, we came to pray for…

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:50.840
Work.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.520
It’s a secret.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:52.480
A secret?

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.020
A secret.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:53.480
A secret?

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:54.560
Yes, I’m not telling.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.540
They said you’re not supposed 
to say your wish out loud.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:58.480
Oh.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.700
This is the windmill temple. Okay.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.680
Let’s go in.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.020
When I was a kid, I came to Hong Kong a lot.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:03.500
Really?

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:04.200
Why?

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.120
I came a lot when I was a kid, too.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:09.800
Why?

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.660
I don’t remember.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:12.960
I don’t remember either.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.100
But I took photos with the “blade building.”

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.020
I have a picture with that building.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.000
I also have a picture, 
but I don’t know what I took it with.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.720
But I was so young.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.540
Like elementary or early middle school.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.980
People have to check in at that “blade building.”

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.700
I think so.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.440
Right? Did you ride the boat?

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.500
And this is the offering kit.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.880
Okay, now that we’re here.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.100
There’s gold paper

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.280
and a windmill.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.880
For borrowing money.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.380
It’s a ritual for borrowing money from the gods.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.060
But you have to return it later, 
otherwise the merit won’t be yours.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:47.520
Yes.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.020
We have to transfer Thai money back 
because we didn’t exchange currency.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:50.560
Yes.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.660
We have to activate the offering first.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:53.780
Where? How?

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.640
Say “Please activate this”?

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:56.500
Yes, please activate it.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.700
(See? She put her IG in there too.)

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:08.820
Oh, you put yours too.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.240
Please follow us, everyone.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.280
Please do.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.380
I was blessed.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.580
I think when we go home, we’ll have tons of work.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.800
We decided not to eat mala because 
we were afraid it’d make us smell, but…

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.420
We’re definitely gonna be rich.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:22.660
(You know, when they activate 
the blessing, they use the powder for it.)

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:23.800
Really?

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.720
(The incense powder got on you.)

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.300
(That means you’ve really “made it.”)

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:30.200
I’ve made it.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:30.860
It got on me.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:31.360
(Yes.)

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.240
Let’s go inside so we can spin the windmill.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.580
We’re done!

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:45.600
(Should we get our fortune read?)

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:46.640
Fortune reading?

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.020
Feels just like Thailand.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.280
We really came all the way today.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.400
Will we understand each other, though?

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:52.960
(How are things today?)

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.540
I feel full of…

00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.200
Good luck?

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.060
Good luck, yes.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.180
(May everyone be blessed.)

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.140
When you go back, 
you won’t be a cameraman anymore.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:07.460
You’ll be a millionaire.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.360
Yeah, we’ll all go back and become millionaires.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.980
Won’t be filming vlogs like this anymore.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.200
(I’ll still do it.)

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.960
We’re gonna go eat.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.180
And get bubble tea.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:20.840
I already requested some desserts.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:21.600
(100% sweetness?)

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.440
Got blessed all over today.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.720
Let’s go eat.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.220
That’s not enough.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:55.960
I can finish that whole thing by myself.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:56.460
(Really?)

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.980
Really. I love this one.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.320
(Nom!)

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.140
Look, I exercise so much I’ve built muscle.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.020
(You work out every day.)

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:33.860
Scary, right?

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.860
Look at my arm first.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.400
Mine is the back of the arm. 
This part is hard to train.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.280
I have muscles too.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.360
Hello.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.620
Hello.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.060
Hello.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.040
Hello, I’m Emi.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.980
Hello, I’m Bonnie.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.240
We’re so excited and happy 
that so many of you came.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:07.460
If you know good places to visit, let us know.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.560
Can we speak enough to live daily life here?

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.820
I can count from 1–99.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.400
But not 100.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.260
Uh… they don’t understand.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:19.100
They don’t.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.880
Yeah, they don’t understand.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.960
Bonnie finished filming super late yesterday.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.520
Does everyone know?

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:42.820
Before coming here, she had to 
go to another province, then go home,

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:45.180
and then go straight to the airport at 9 a.m.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.340
So I was sad.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.140
Sad?

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:48.520
Washing my hair made me sad.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:51.360
Her hair was super extra.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.300
There were so many pins stuck in it.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:55.100
When I washed my hair, I kept finding pins,

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:55.700
one after another,

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:56.700
like ten of them.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.080
So then?

00:09:58.660 --> 00:09:59.260
I cried.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:09:59.920
Cried?

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.520
Like, “When is this going to end?”

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:03.940
Yes.

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.300
And I only slept two hours.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:07.120
So I showered and cried at the same time.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.220
Not full-on crying, but tearing up.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:13.940
If this afternoon were your day off,

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:16.360
what would you most want to do with each other?

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.440
We went on an outing once, 
and I stole P’Mi’s blanket.

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:25.500
And she had to use a towel as a blanket.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:27.980
I want to go to Hong Kong Disneyland.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:32.140
Yeah.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.240
That's it.

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:37.080
At first, we were going to go, 
but I had some work, so we couldn’t.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.020
She had a big mission.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.940
I was sad. I wanted to go.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.220
This one. P’Mi loves eating Peking duck.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.800
Peking duck uses the phone.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:48.940
Yes.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.180
What do you call Peking duck again?

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:57.760
There’s dim sum too. There's everything.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.240
Peking duck, too. Whoa~

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:03.580
Because you’re sweeter than watermelon.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:06.920
That can mean many things.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:09.100
Watermelon is not sweet anymore.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:10.920
When I’m with you.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.320
Because I’m sweeter?

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:12.740
Yeah.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:46.740
It’s Bonnie!

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.140
Bonnie! Bonnie!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.400
And that’s the end! 

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:48.320
of our first fan meeting in Hong Kong!

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:50.760
It was so much fun today.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.000
The fans were so sweet.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.160
Yes, the fans’ energy was amazing.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:54.900
Yes.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:55.820
We can go to the next place anytime.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:56.980
Yes, bring it on.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.340
Or we can do a second one here.

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:58.580
Yes.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:01.580
We don’t mind repeating it.

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.000
For 2, 3, 4, 5 times. We don’t mind.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.060
EmiBonnie Around the World!

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:04.760
Around the World!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.640
Okay, today was so much fun.

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:08.980
The fans were so lovely. 

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.500
Thank you for welcoming us so warmly.

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:12.720
See you again.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:13.300
Yes.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.320
Bye-bye.

